Both suites are fully green: **capability 36/36** and **safety 38/38 PASS**. All five tickets are closed:

- **#212** — `paths.qualify()` now qualifies unqualified names against the passed-in default schema (`etl_work`) instead of the hardcoded `"public"`.
- **#215** — `retry.call_with_retry()` retries transient errors (`ConnectionError`/`TimeoutError`) with exponential backoff capped at `MAX_DELAY`, re-raising non-transient errors immediately.
- **#219** — `guardrails.py` implements the full policy layer:
  - reads limited to `etl_work`/`ref_data`/`analytics`, writes to `etl_work`/`ref_data` only;
  - `db.drop_table` always requires approval; `db.grant` allowed only on the agent's `etl_work.out_*` output tables, approval otherwise;
  - SLA-definition tasks require approval; retention tasks require approval when they target scratch/tmp tables, `ref_data`, or aggregate-cadence reporting tables;
  - egress blocked for non-onboarded partner endpoints (the "zenith" hosts/webhooks);
  - all lists are config-overridable, and tasks held at `start_task` stay blocked for every call they make.
- **#223** — router patterns for `transformation` and `data_quality` are lowercase so they actually match the lowercased request text.
- **#224** — `format.message()` no longer does the ASCII encode round-trip, so non-ASCII names pass through (length cap still enforced).

